# BlitzArt Linux -- live session

This directory is copied onto the ISO. To install BlitzArt to a disk:

    sudo blitzinstall

(the `blitzinstall` command starts install-1.sh; it is also on PATH as
/usr/local/bin/blitzinstall on the live ISO).

Live session user:  blitz / blitz

Files here:
  install-1.sh         stage 1: partitioning, btrfs, system copy, calls stage 2
  install-2.sh         stage 2: config, repos, GRUB, snapper, zram, services
  install-dotfiles.sh  optional dotfiles installer (asked during stage 2)
  blitz                system toolbox (also installed into the target system)
  blitzinstall         wrapper that starts install-1.sh (also installed as
                       /usr/local/bin/blitzinstall into the target system)

The installed system is BlitzArt Linux: btrfs + snapper snapshots in the GRUB
menu, zram swap, dinit services, blitz toolbox. Reboot after stage 2 finishes.
